{"file":"Ngrok Agent Skills-1.0.0-v1.zip","bytes":83520,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"skills","description":"ngrok Agent Skills collection: expose localhost, secure endpoints, receive webhooks, and more.","version":"1.0.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/ngrok/skills","homepage":"https://github.com/ngrok/skills"},{"path":".cursor-plugin/plugin.json","name":"skills","displayName":"ngrok Skills","description":"ngrok Agent Skills collection: expose localhost, secure endpoints, receive webhooks, and more.","version":"1.0.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/ngrok/skills","homepage":"https://github.com/ngrok/skills","keywords":["ngrok","connectivity","gateway","networking","localhost"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/expose-localhost/SKILL.md","name":"expose-localhost","description":"Expose a local service to the public internet using ngrok. Starts a tunnel, optionally adds OAuth or WAF via Traffic Policy. Handles HTTP services and raw TCP (SSH, RDP, databases). Use when asked to expose, tunnel, share, or make a local service publicly accessible, or to reach a machine that has no public IP. Also covers sharing work-in-progress with a specific person and the dev-server quirks that break a shared preview.","headings":["Expose Localhost","Prerequisites","Workflow","Step 1: Pre-flight & Configuration","Step 2: Start the Tunnel","Step 3: Handle Errors","Step 4: Persistent Configuration (If Requested)","Teardown","Non-HTTP Services (TCP)","local sshd on port 22, reached through the address above","Cloud Endpoints (Advanced)","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"expose · localhost"},{"path":"skills/ngrok-engine/SKILL.md","name":"ngrok-engine","description":"Reference for ngrok's traffic model - what an endpoint is and what happens to traffic at the edge. Covers endpoint types (agent, cloud, internal), bindings and protocols (HTTP, TLS, TCP), and Traffic Policy - the YAML rule language of phases, CEL expressions, and actions, with a generated catalog of all 26 actions. Other ngrok skills point here to decide what to build, then to ngrok-surfaces to apply it. Not a standalone task - load when another skill references it.","headings":["The ngrok engine: endpoints and Traffic Policy","1. Endpoint type","2. Traffic Policy","The action vocabulary","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"ngrok · engine"},{"path":"skills/ngrok-setup/SKILL.md","name":"ngrok-setup","description":"Get authenticated and ready to use ngrok on whatever surface the task needs - agent CLI, an SDK, or infrastructure-as-code. Detects what is already installed, walks the one-time authtoken step, and routes to the right surface. Use before other ngrok tasks, or whenever an ngrok command fails with an authentication or configuration error. Use when the user says \"set up ngrok\", \"install ngrok\", \"add my authtoken\", \"ngrok isn't authenticated\", or \"getting an auth error from ngrok\".","headings":["Set up ngrok","1. Figure out the surface","2. Authenticate","3. Make sure the tool is present","4. Hand back","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"ngrok · 设置"},{"path":"skills/ngrok-surfaces/SKILL.md","name":"ngrok-surfaces","description":"How to apply an ngrok endpoint and Traffic Policy on whichever surface the user is actually working in - the agent CLI and ngrok.yml, the ngrok SDKs (Go, JavaScript, Python, Rust), the REST API at api.ngrok.com, the Terraform provider, and the Kubernetes Operator. Routes from signals in the user's project to the right surface, then to that surface's reference file. Other ngrok skills point here once they know what to build. Not a standalone task - load when another skill references it.","headings":["Applying ngrok on the user's surface","Pick the surface","The axis that actually separates them","Auth differs by surface","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"ngrok · surfaces"},{"path":"skills/provision-sandbox-access/SKILL.md","name":"provision-sandbox-access","description":"Give every sandbox, container, device, or tenant its own isolated ngrok endpoint, provisioned programmatically at runtime from a controlplane. Covers the per-workload resource set - service user, reserved address or domain, ACL-scoped authtoken, cloud endpoint forwarding to a private internal endpoint - plus the agent config that runs inside the workload, and teardown. Use when the user is building a platform that spins up isolated environments.","headings":["Provision isolated access per sandbox","Before you start","The shape","1. Derive a stable identifier","2. Create the identity and address","3. Mint a credential that can do exactly one thing","4. Create the cloud endpoint","5. Configure the agent inside the workload","Tear it down","Scenarios","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"provision · sandbox · access"},{"path":"skills/receive-webhooks/SKILL.md","name":"receive-webhooks","description":"Receive and verify inbound webhooks from providers like Stripe, GitHub, Twilio, Slack, or Shopify and deliver them to a local or private service without exposing that service to the public internet. Verify signatures at the edge with no app code; route third-party callbacks to a service behind a firewall, including regulated (HIPAA/PCI) environments or a centralized webhook gateway shared across teams. Use when the user needs to receive, test, or debug webhooks locally, wants signature verification without writing it, or must route callbacks to a private service.","headings":["Receive webhooks","Before you start","Core pattern (every case)","Choose the shape","Apply it","Worked scenarios (same mechanism, different emphasis)","Verify it works","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"receive · webhooks"},{"path":"skills/run-mcp-gateway/SKILL.md","name":"run-mcp-gateway","description":"Expose an in-development MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for remote testing against AI model providers like Claude and OpenAI, with per-provider authentication and traffic inspection. Puts a cloud endpoint in front of your local MCP server, authenticates each provider with its own bearer [已隐藏] via Vaults, and forwards to your server kept off the public internet. Use when the user is building or testing an MCP server and needs a remote AI client to reach it. Use when the user says \"test my MCP server\", \"expose my MCP server to Claude\", \"connect my MCP server to OpenAI\", or \"front door for my MCP server\".","headings":["Run an MCP gateway","Before you start","Architecture","Steps","Gotchas","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"run · mcp · gateway"},{"path":"skills/secure-endpoint/SKILL.md","name":"secure-endpoint","description":"Put authentication, rate limiting, IP restrictions, header rules, or a custom response in front of an ngrok endpoint using a Traffic Policy, without changing application code. Covers requiring login (OAuth/OIDC), locking to specific IPs, blocking or denying requests, returning a maintenance page or custom response, and injecting or stripping headers. Use when the user wants to protect, gate, throttle, or add an API-gateway layer to an endpoint. Use when the user says \"add auth to my ngrok URL\", \"require Google login\", \"rate limit my endpoint\", \"restrict by IP\", \"block a path\", or \"put up a maintenance page\".","headings":["Secure an endpoint","Before you start","Scenarios","Require login (OAuth / OIDC)","Lock to specific IPs","Block a path or condition (deny)","Rate limit","Maintenance page / custom response","Add / strip headers","Combining","Apply it","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"secure · endpoint"},{"path":"skills/troubleshoot-ngrok/SKILL.md","name":"troubleshoot-ngrok","description":"Diagnose and fix common ngrok errors and connection problems - offline endpoints (ERR_NGROK_3200), agent authentication and connection failures, upstream/tunnel connection refused, and Traffic Policy errors. Reads the error code and explains the specific cause and fix. Use when an ngrok URL returns an error, a tunnel won't come up, or the agent reports a connection problem. Use when the user says \"ngrok says endpoint offline\", \"ERR_NGROK_3200\", \"my tunnel isn't working\", \"why is my ngrok URL down\", or pastes an ngrok error code.","headings":["Troubleshoot ngrok","First: get the code","High-frequency codes","By symptom (no code)","Notes for agents"],"name_hint":"排查 · ngrok"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["ngrok Agent Skills","Getting Started","Installation","What It Does","Skills","Supporting References","Usage","Architecture","License"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".cursor-plugin/marketplace.json",".cursor-plugin/plugin.json",".gitignore","LICENSE","README.md","skills/expose-localhost/SKILL.md","skills/expose-localhost/references/TROUBLESHOOTING.md","skills/ngrok-engine/SKILL.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/action-catalog.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/add-headers.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/basic-auth.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/circuit-breaker.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/close-connection.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/compress-response.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/custom-response.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/deny.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/forward-internal.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/http-request.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/jwt-validation.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/log.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/oauth.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/oidc.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/owasp-crs-request.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/owasp-crs-response.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/rate-limit.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/redirect.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/remove-headers.md","skills/ngrok-engine/references/actions/request-body-find-replace.md","skill